KZ3 patch 2161 (ENHANCEMENT, experimental): feed FSR from the deferred scene rather than the depthless scanout.

A metadata-only gameplay capture established that the four-target full-resolution deferred pass owns the usable
depth, while the alternating display surfaces receive a later depthless composition. Select that MRT pass
structurally, apply the same temporal jitter to it and depth-tested scene draws, and carry its current-frame depth
to presentation. No unidentified MRT is treated as velocity.

The PPU flip clock and the live renderer's frame counter are not lockstep. Snapshot the latest coherent camera when
the primary deferred draw is processed and reuse that exact snapshot for both jitter and presentation instead of
comparing unrelated counters.

The validated scene target is first filled from the deferred-lighting target and then receives blended forward
draws before its existing local-to-main post-chain copy. Capture that target after the opaque resolve and again
immediately before the copy. Strict frame, target, resource, dimensions, and FSR-context keys decide whether the
port-owned adapter may generate a reactive mask from the pair. Missing or mismatched captures leave the mask
optional; an expected adapter dispatch failure still follows the existing explicit Bilinear fallback.

The selection and matching rules live in port/kz3/fsr31_inputs.h and are covered by
tools/smoke/test_fsr31_inputs.c. This patch contains no game code or assets.

